# Cell from playpick: mode=walk, boss=saved, spec=warlock:destruction,
# style=dodge, size=10, difficulty=normal, view=1280x800, save=fresh.
#
# "walk" means the long way (no #hash shortcut): front page -> RAID -> class
# pick -> WALK IN. boss=saved (The One You Save) is a coverage label only --
# evening steers at no boss -- but it names a target worth checking: no
# session in this job's history has ever actually reached or fought "saved".
# It sits in room `dream`, the first fight of the frostwing wing, which from
# a fresh door is threshold -> vigil -> spire(marrow) -> climb -> oratory
# (whisper) -> mooring(skyward) -> rise(gorged) -> crossing -> dream(saved) --
# four boss fights and the whole lower spire before the target is even in
# range. direction.md's hypothesis 6 has `dodge` at 3-for-3 clean THE VIGIL
# crossings (never once stalled), and #271's wipe-retry bug is closed, so
# this is the first session positioned to actually walk that far rather than
# die or stall at the first corridor. warlock:destruction has been walked
# before under melee (wiped at VIGIL, #271-era) and wander (also wiped,
# #271-era) on this exact size/difficulty/save/view cell -- dodge is the one
# style never tried on this spec, and a controlled same-cell comparison
# against those two prior wipes.
open
targets
ui
shot front
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:warlock:destruction
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot arrive-threshold
state
targets

# Chunk 1: threshold -> vigil -> spire(marrow) -> climb -> oratory(whisper) ->
# mooring(skyward)/rise(gorged). Evening stops itself early (evening-stuck) if
# two rooms in a row go nowhere; budget kept inside one foreground invocation.
evening dodge 150 6
shot after-evening-1
state
says
bill
targets
